description: Always tell the user when pushing, opening/updating a PR, or merging
alwaysApply: true
---

# Notify on push / PR / merge

Whenever you **push** to a remote, **create** a PR, **update** a PR (description / draft→ready / URL), **merge** a PR, or **delete** a remote branch, tell the user in the same turn:

- What you did (push / open PR / update PR / merge / delete branch)
- Branch name
- PR URL (if any)
- Short what landed (1 line)

Do this even when the push/PR/merge was already authorized by `ok` / workflow SOP. Never silently push, open a PR, or merge.
